  <h1>On-Policy Distillation Done Right:<br>Three Failure Modes and One Fix</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    Standard on-policy distillation asks a teacher to grade <em>one sampled token</em> per prefix—but that single comparison is imbalanced, fooled by repetition, and corrupted by tokenizer mismatches.
    Teacher top-K local support matching replaces the one-token signal with a truncated KL over a teacher-selected support set, and delivers a <strong>+19.8% math reasoning improvement</strong> with no architectural changes.
  </p>
